    narrativeReview: "We approached the menu board, queued, and eventually reached the till, where we were welcomed by Lily. They greeted us in a polite and professional manner before asking what we would like to order. Before proceeding with the order, they asked whether we had any allergies. I asked whether gluten-free options were available, and they clarified whether gluten was a preference or an allergy. I explained that I was asking on behalf of somebody else rather than for myself. They then explained that gluten-free options were available, although not every item on the menu could be prepared as gluten-free. They also referred to the allergen folder, which contained detailed information about the menu items and their allergens, allowing visitors to make an informed choice. We ordered a chicken burger and a burrito. The waiting time was approximately ten minutes, after which the food was presented on a tray for collection. Once we had collected our meal, we used the self-service condiment station, which was clean, well organised and fully stocked with ketchup, mayonnaise, mustard, salt, pepper and napkins. From a service perspective, Lily communicated clearly, followed the allergy procedure appropriately and demonstrated good product knowledge by explaining the available dietary options. They ensured that the relevant information was provided before the order was completed, which contributed to a professional and reassuring interaction. From a food quality perspective, my experience was mixed. The chicken burger contained what appeared to be a genuine chicken breast rather than processed meat, which I appreciated. It was freshly prepared, not greasy and of a noticeably better quality than I had anticipated for a quick-service offering within a visitor attraction. In contrast, the fries were only average in quality. They were not served particularly hot and did not have the crispness or freshness I would have expected, making them less enjoyable. The burrito was presented well; however, I found it considerably spicier than anticipated. Although I personally enjoy spicy food, the level of heat was significantly higher than I would consider suitable for the average visitor. Given that the attraction welcomes families and international visitors with a wide range of preferences, I felt that the spice level may not appeal to many guests unless it was clearly indicated in advance. The staff member I spoke about the QR code was male, 1.70m, short black hair and black eyes",
